  1621                                  ; unless [quiet], a message.
  1622                                  ;
  1623                                  ; One burst: the preamble, the CMD24 frame and its window (R1 arrives in
  1624                                  ; it), FF FE -- the token, a byte at least after R1 -- the 512 bytes, their
  1625                                  ; CRC16, and WRESP bytes of FF in which the card's data response comes.
  1626                                  ; R1 locates the offset; the response is the first byte after the CRC, at
  1627                                  ; it, that is not FF, and must say "accepted" (xxx0 0101).  Then the card
  1628                                  ; holds DO low while it programs, polled in bursts of its own (busy is all
  1629                                  ; 0s: the offset does not matter) until a word of FFFF.  Then CMD13, the
  1630                                  ; card's status, must be 00 00.
